seg-6144da0bfed4 = Pick a site, a time and a mix of global navigation satellite systems (GNSS) and a low Earth orbit (LEO) layer, draw the skyline that blocks your view, and see the dilution of precision (DOP) and the position error it implies. Every number comes from the Kshana engine running in this browser. <a1>What this shows</a1>.

# tools/index.html
seg-61e5733012cf = The Norwegian Jammertest publishes a test catalogue and a transmission plan. Kshana reads them as <b>scheduled truth</b>, the slots the plan says, not recorded on-air times, and scores a receiver-trust run against them: per test, was it detected, how late, did it recover, and which alarms fell outside every slot. Choose the catalogue and plan files you downloaded yourself (Kshana does not bundle them) and a receiver log. Everything runs in this browser; nothing is uploaded.

