seg-a11e88108e1c = <b>The error ellipse</b> is the horizontal error from the geometry's covariance, σ<s1>UERE</s1>² times the east-north block of the DOP matrix: longer along the directions the satellites constrain least. It is drawn at 1-sigma and at { "95" } % ({ "2.448" } times larger). <b>The Monte Carlo cloud</b> is many least-squares solutions with seeded random range errors through the same geometry; its RMS is shown beside σ<s2>UERE</s2> × HDOP, with the share of points inside the { "95" } % ellipse. The same seed always gives the same cloud.

